{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes","id":1041713,"title":"Truth in Mage and D&D Planes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T23:22:54-08:00","id":1041713,"title":"Truth in Mage and D&D Planes","content":"Inside <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues\">Wisdom Issues</a> discussion came interesting subtopic about how <b>Mage</b> Supernal and Abyss relate to <b>D&amp;D </b>Great Wheel cosmology. Here is sum up of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues?p=1041049#post1041049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Mage) Abyss is not 'evil'. It's <i>Chaos</i>. Primordial Chaos. And like in D&amp;D or Warhammer - from this Chaos comes Order. Supernal ( in form of Arcana ) is all about ( secret ) Order to universe. There are hierarchies of power ( Gnosis ), there are levels of initiation (Arcana). Heck, even Supernal World could be said to work as 'putting in to boxes' most chaotic thing like 'magic based on all possible Symbols'. Like in <b>Left Hand Path</b> book chapter on Scelesti - For Fallen World to exist in semi-constant manner ( or exist in any meaningful way ) Order needed to win over Chaos. But just like <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Chaos_Gods_of_Law\" target=\"_blank\">Law gods of Warhammer universe are only (most powerful ) faction in all Chaos gods</a>, so can be said Supernal is most 'logical' or 'ordered' parts of Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues?p=1041195#post1041195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To continue this line of thought... Were you all aware that in D&amp;D, all of creation may have sprang from the Chaotic Evil realm of the Abyss as well? And that doesn't stop the Abyss in that game from being tied to evil actions and destruction in order to drag creation back into the chaos of the bottomless Abyss?<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, there's no &quot;Evil&quot; label in the CofD, but other than that, there's actually a wealth of things that the two have in common if you look beyond just the evil-for-evil-sake's cartoonish portrayal that sometimes shows up. Its amazing how much D&amp;D!Abyss and CofD!Abyss have in common. Hmm.... would that make the Exarchs the equivalent to the Archdevils? They're both divine embodiments of tyranny... I'll have to think more on that one later.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues?p=1041381#post1041381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mount Celestia has multiple layers, where how enlightened you are determines on which layer you stand. Hmm... Where have I red about something like this before?<br /> <br /> Also, Abyss is probably more like D&amp;D Far Realms. Demons seem to be more like CofD Akathartoi.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues?p=1041418#post1041418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those would be the Devils, given their approach (trying to corrupt through contracts and subtle influence).<br /> <br /> D&amp;D demons with their rampant and wanton destruction could definitely fit other Lower Depths realms</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1036789-wisdom-issues?p=1041542#post1041542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The original D&amp;D Abyss included all the abomination overlords, including mindflayer and abolith gods. The far realm eventually co-opted that, but at the heart, there are still demon lords based on the same things as the Far Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>For those that do not know D&amp;D, here is simple drawings of it cosmology.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/4WJpdBN.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In a nutshell, universe in D&amp;D is divided on Inner ( Elemental ) and Outer ( Philosophical ) Planes \u2013 i.e. various \u2018Realms\u2019 of Mage gameline. Those Outer Planes are looking very much as more basic Supernal Realms. One of it is Abyss \u2013 bottomless Plane of Chaotic Evil \u2013 that in above discussion was equated to Mage\u2019s Void. In lore of D&amp;D all Outer Planes are coming from it\u2019s Abyss, and the same can be said in Mage.<br /> <br /> Gist here is that those mapped Outer Planes are to be \u2018most common\u2019 to characters in D&amp;D \u2013 lore says there are countless other, just outside perception. In the same way, Supernal Realms of Paths in Mage are those where Watchtowers were erected being \u2018most close\u2019 to the center of Mage \u2018Great Wheel\u2019. What\u2019s even more interesting \u2013 interpreting as everything coming from Mage Void/Abyss ( like Abyss of D&amp;D ) would mean that all Awakened, in reality, are Scelesti, just those from Paths are more \u2018ordered\u2019. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:35:22-08:00","id":1041717,"title":"","content":"Considering the Abyss amongst the various otherworlds is what mages used to do, right?<br /> <br /> Still, I'm not so sure about the Outer Planes being equal to the Supernal Realms themselves, since you can still physically visit the former with a little aid from planar travel magic, while the latter can only be 'visited' by transfiguring yourself into an abstract concept. Maybe particularly focused Emanations?<br /> <br /> Or maybe, this is all how it used to work in the Time Before, before the Abyss-That-Is-Not-The-Abyss rose up to crash the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T00:54:26-08:00","id":1041728,"title":"","content":"I feel like describing the abyss as representing &quot;chaos&quot; and the Supernal as representing &quot;order&quot; is at all accurate. The symbols of disorder, dissolution, anarchy, formlessness... all the things we associate with the word &quot;chaos&quot; exist within the Supernal Realms. The Abyss consists of things that that do not exist yet hunger for existence; lies that hunger to make themselves true. While Abyssal Incursions manifest themselves through more or less familiar things that make up the world and reflect the truths of the Supernal, their core nature is fundamentally outside of reality as we know it. Predatory histories that seek to consume the timeline we know, sentient diseases that utterly obliterate the ability to communicate and understand communication, irrefutable proofs that undermine even the most basic principals of physics - the abyss represents not primordial chaos, but the antithesis of truth, understanding, and *being* itself.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's a tricky distinction to make, but I think it's a crucial one. To suggest that the cosmos, or just the Supernal, is in some way part of the Abyss is, I think, to fundamentally misunderstand what the abyss is. Indeed, to a certain extent the only consistent definition of the Abyss is &quot;that which is no part of the worlds we know.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the Abyss in D&amp;D... well, the forces of evil and chaos like to make all sorts of claims about the nature of the universe, but those same beings are the very definition of an unreliable source. There are alternative stories which assert that the universe began as place of perfect order, and perhaps even perfect goodness, but that part of it have become corrupt and degenerated over time. Why should we favor the word of demons over... well... literally anyone else in the Planes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 02-01-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:03:39-08:00","id":1041730,"title":"","content":"I was looking at the similarities the other day as well and their are alot. D&amp;D's alignment system aside the Outer Planes all had values that governed how magic worked to fit the magical outlook of the plane. And if nothing else use the manes and through the rest out the window.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:12:05-08:00","id":1041731,"title":"","content":"If you incorporate 4e cosmology and/or the parts of it 5e stole and adoped into its revised version of Great Wheel, you've also got the Shadowfell and the Feywild, which kinda vaguely resemble the Shadow and the Hedge/Faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:17:57-08:00","id":1041735,"title":"","content":"I agree, Like was mentioned there are alot of similarities. Yes D&amp;D calls them planes of existence, Mage calls them realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:25:03-08:00","id":1041737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041728#post1041728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Abyssal Incursions manifest themselves through more or less familiar things that make up the world and reflect the truths of the Supernal, their core nature is fundamentally outside of reality as we know it. Predatory histories that seek to consume the timeline we know, sentient diseases that utterly obliterate the ability to communicate and understand communication, irrefutable proofs that undermine even the most basic principals of physics - the abyss represents not primordial chaos, but the antithesis of truth, understanding, and *being* itself.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's a tricky distinction to make, but I think it's a crucial one. To suggest that the cosmos, or just the Supernal, is in some way part of the Abyss is, I think, to fundamentally misunderstand what the abyss is. Indeed, to a certain extent the only consistent definition of the Abyss is &quot;that which is no part of the worlds we know.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>do not</b> point that particular Abyssal Beings are only representations of Chaos or that Supernal do not have Symbols of anarchy and a like. I point that Abyss <i>is</i> 'great sea of everything', from that other things comes. It's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Mesopotamian_religion#Mythology\" target=\"_blank\">corpse of Tiamat from that Marduk created our one world.</a> It's <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/tales/norse-creation-myth/\" target=\"_blank\">Ginnungagap and giant Yamir that created world for the Norse</a>. Each Abyssal being is discreet entity that want to 'live' in Fallen World - and each Annanuki is whole world that want to overwritten our Fallen World to become one 'being', in contrast to each other of it's siblings.<br /> <br /> <b>Void/Abyss in Mage is not (simply) 'Chaotic Evil' - it's just first ( and probably last ) point in universe creation. Abyss in Mage has EVERYTHING in it - just more stable parts of reality we call Fallen World, and they fight ( in Abyss ) over what is 'stable' now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T02:02:33-08:00","id":1041742,"title":"","content":"I still wouldn't say that the Abyss is the Primordial, but rather that it is the Outside. The Primordial, like you point out, exist at the Alpha &amp; Omega of reality, making it conceptually closest to the stillborn gods and corpses of world-progenitors that lie Outside reality. Therefore, the anti-beings of the Abyss find it the easiest to piggyback on the resonances of those belonging to the Primordial - hence all those chaotic, evil, destructive and perverted phenomena.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think Mage Abyss corresponds to the Far Planes.<br /> <br /> Consequently, I think the closest thing DnD Abyss corresponds to in CofD is the Primordial Dream. Greed, tyranny, pain, punishment, and despair as a fundamental part of the universe? Sounds a lot like how the evil Outer Planes are still a part of reality, and how Evil is a cosmic force in DnD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T05:41:56-08:00","id":1041775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041742#post1041742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wouldn't say that the Abyss is the Primordial, but rather that it is the Outside. The Primordial, like you point out, exist at the Alpha &amp; Omega of reality, making it conceptually closest to the stillborn gods and corpses of world-progenitors that lie Outside reality. Therefore, the anti-beings of the Abyss find it the easiest to piggyback on the resonances of those belonging to the Primordial - hence all those chaotic, evil, destructive and perverted phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your Outside is still about stillborn gods and corpses of world-progenitors, then you say the same as I think Primodrial in this sense. I.E. 'Place where universe as we know it started - and things that 'did not catch' with those that made Fallen World.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041742#post1041742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I think Mage Abyss corresponds to the Far Planes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean that D&amp;D Great Wheal is coming from Far Planes, and Far is 'all around' the Wheel, then we agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T05:50:37-08:00","id":1041777,"title":"","content":"Now looking over forum, I think I made the same points on Mage Abyss few months before. We have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-%E2%80%98growing%E2%80%99-with-humanity\">proofs that Supernal is evolving with humanity</a> - that lead that nowadays Supernal was Not-Supernal before humans. And Not-Supernal is <i>definition</i> of Abyss, so we have proof that 'First Atlantis' <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-%E2%80%98ordered%E2%80%99-abyss\">changed portions of Abyss in to stable and evolving Supernal Realms</a> by seeding Watchtowers - and creating Paths by this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:04:55-08:00","id":1041782,"title":"","content":"No, the Far Realm is a place completely outside of the Great Wheel - essentially a completely different cosmos that bumped into the Great Wheel and parts of its reality began to bleed into the reality of the Great Wheel. Creatures from the Far Realm are completely alien to all of the Planes, and inherently destructive to them, because they are native to a different reality that is incompatible with the reality of the Great Wheel.<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>, the Far Realm is a much closer anologue for Mage's Abyss than the D&amp;D Abyss is. Mage's Abyss isn't a place of primordial chaos from which the universe as we know it immerged, it is a separate unreality from which impossible things bleed into our own reality, which is inherently destructive to our own reality because they are incompatible with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:09:04-08:00","id":1041804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041782#post1041782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage's Abyss isn't a place of primordial chaos from which the universe as we know it immerged,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Scelesti section of Left-Hand Path suggests exactly that. That doesn't make it right, but it's certainly a valid option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:13:41-08:00","id":1041807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041804#post1041804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Scelesti section of Left-Hand Path suggests exactly that. That doesn't make it right, but it's certainly a valid option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ok, I haven't read that. Still, that's not how it's typically presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:34:28-08:00","id":1041823,"title":"","content":"The abyss is everything that doesn't exist. The universe didn't actually emerge from the abyss, so the abyss <i>is </i>the thing it emerged from.<br /> <br /> If the universe <i>had</i> emerged from the abyss, then it wouldn't have. Which it didn't. So it did.<br /> <br /> I've gone cross-eyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-01-2017, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:03:38-08:00","id":1041832,"title":"","content":"Remembers me of that nice logic Problem:<br /> No cat has two tails.<br /> One cat has one more tail than no cat.<br /> Consequently every cat has three tails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:31:06-08:00","id":1041842,"title":"","content":"Going with Abyss as Primodrial Chaos / Starting Darkness is in themes with many religions. Just see this paragraph on <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/cosmology/ginnungagap/\" target=\"_blank\">site dedicated to Norse mythology</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/learn-old-norse/\" target=\"_blank\">Old Norse</a> word <i>gap</i> means the same thing as it does in modern English: a void, an empty space. The meaning of the <i>ginnung</i> element, however, is far less certain. The best guess anyone has come up with so far is Jan de Vries\u2019s suggestion of \u201c<a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/concepts/magic/\" target=\"_blank\">magically</a>-charged,\u201d<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[2]</span></span> a theory that has gained widespread acceptance.<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[3]</span></span> This would certainly be in keeping with the interpretations propounded below.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Chaos and Cosmos</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This perfect, uninterrupted silence and darkness has close counterparts in other mythologies from around the world. To cite but one example, most of my readers will no doubt be familiar with the famous words of the first chapter of <i>Genesis</i>, which describe the state of the universe prior to the intervention of Elohim in Judeo-Christian mythology: \u201cAnd the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep.\u201d The opposition between the well-ordered, just, and beneficent cosmos on the one hand and the lawless chaos that surrounds it is perhaps one of the most common themes in religion and in human consciousness more generally.<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[4]</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the pre-Christian religion of the Norse and other Germanic peoples, this chaos-cosmos split is expressed as an opposition between the <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/concepts/innangard-and-utangard/\" target=\"_blank\">innangard</a>, that which is orderly, civilized, and law-abiding, and the <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/concepts/innangard-and-utangard/\" target=\"_blank\">utangard</a>, that which is wild and anarchic. Plowed fields are innangard, but beyond the fences that surround them and mark them off reigns the wilderness, the utangard home of the <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/gods-and-creatures/giants/\" target=\"_blank\">giants</a>. These anti-cosmic forces are constantly trying to drag the <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/gods-and-creatures/the-aesir-gods-and-goddesses/\" target=\"_blank\">Aesir</a> gods, their work, and their ideals back to chaos (and at Ragnarok they succeed, at least for a time). While the wilderness is utangard enough, the \u201ccapital\u201d of chaos, as it were, is Ginnungagap; the abyss is the ultimate destination to which the giants want to bring the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> But probably <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">Elfive</a> is right - Abyss is so contradicting it both can be and not be source of universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Side topic: NOW I understand why canonical Scelestus has taken name of Norse giantess Angerboda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:08:25-08:00","id":1041892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041842#post1041842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side topic: NOW I understand why canonical Scelestus has taken name of Norse giantess Angerboda. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That name basically means &quot;Mother of monsters&quot; he took it because he was a member of Legion and was therefore hosting a whole bunch of Gulmoth inside his body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:23:14-08:00","id":1041901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes#post1041713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s even more interesting \u2013 interpreting as everything coming from Mage Void/Abyss ( like Abyss of D&amp;D ) would mean that all Awakened, in reality, are Scelesti, just those from Paths are more \u2018ordered\u2019. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. I've been thinking about this myself for the past few weeks. It seems like you originally just have the Abyss, the primordial chaos full of everything. Someone, somewhere in the Abyss, decides they want the one thing the Abyss doesn't have. Order. Or Law. Structure. This is not the Order of Law of Dungeons and Dragons and Warhammer, this is language from random noise. And suddenly, the framework is done. Rules are set down, the Matrix is created, designed to keep the place stable-ish. The Abyss is out there, always, some want to destroy the world, some want to get in there, to see what the hubbub is all about, some want to matter, but the vast majority doesn't care.<br /> <br /> If you cling to the idea that humanity empowers the supernal watchtowers, then view the watchtowers as the foundation of this fake world. They make the rules, they're the macros and underlying code language that allow everything else in the Fallen world to Exist.<br /> <br /> The mages of 'Atlantis' if there really was such a thing, would be Abyss-born, but not necessarily Scelesti, as they wanted something else. Scelesti deny the Supernal, and most every mage, even the Seers, serve it, so they wouldn't be Scelesti.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you could go the other way. Whatever created the world made a rule, 'This is not a part of the world,' and in doing so, created This, in the form of the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:09:48-08:00","id":1041931,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, generally I agree with your POV - I only mark 'All magic is from Abyss' to show two things:<br /> 1. To have reason for other mages to join Scelsti - if all magic comes from the Abyss, only Supernal part is 'artificially' limited - then let Abyss make your dark miracles and 'save Padme', if my Arcana cannot do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=05dT34hGRdg\" data-code=\"05dT34hGRdg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/05dT34hGRdg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> 2. Magic is WILD - it <i>want</i>'s to control you. Arcana maybe have hierarchies and are all based on various levels of understanding - but in the end, they are this powerful force that want's to control you, than be tamed. Maybe it's the residue of hailing from Abyss at the dawn of time, maybe it's it own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:17:59-08:00","id":1041934,"title":"","content":"I believe Supernal magic's influence on humans is more related to how mages Awaken to it, with possibly some further influence from Exarchs and the symbolic power of the Order.<br /> <br /> There's more to things, too. Chronicles has long been giving nods towards Gnosticism, and it stands to reason that the Fallen World is not the only world, just a reflection of the 'true' one that was created. For all we know it might go on and on like that, 'turtles all the way down' so to speak, into the lower depths and alternative 'fallen worlds' and on and on. But at that point can you really theorize about it, since it's so beyond anything in the world it wouldn't get much more than a brief glimpse even in meta content.<br /> <br /> But oh yes, certainly the advantage of the scelesti is that you can do things that are impossible, even for mages. The problem is it's hard, now, to get study for that going. There's a lot of bad out there with a lot of good, and it would take a long time to gather the information you'd need to make sure you limited the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Z\u0328\u0316\u0316\u033b\u0325a\u0316lg\u035f\u0333o\u0327\u034d\u033c\u033a\u0319\u031f\u032b\u0332 </span></span>that would otherwise come through. And with the current mage structure, which is heavily anti-Abyss, you probably couldn't get that research done. And so many Scelesti fall into traps, not trying to do impossible magic but following a specific legacy or going for one goal, rather than a general study of things.<br /> <br /> But since the Abyss is denigrated, that's not likely to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T11:49:23-08:00","id":1041941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041934#post1041934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's more to things, too. Chronicles has long been giving nods towards Gnosticism, and it stands to reason that the Fallen World is not the only world, just a reflection of the 'true' one that was created. For all we know it might go on and on like that, 'turtles all the way down' so to speak, into the lower depths and alternative 'fallen worlds' and on and on. But at that point can you really theorize about it, since it's so beyond anything in the world it wouldn't get much more than a brief glimpse even in meta content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I got idea that our ( real world ) Earth is 'true' representation that CoD Fallen World try to mimic, but with pollution of Abyss and other dark forces we end up with whole 'and more people are missing, more murders are made and world is a bit more darker than ours'... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:02:36-08:00","id":1041980,"title":"","content":"If I understand it correctly, the idea that the universe (in the broadest possible sense) emerged from the Abyss goes something like this: &quot;before the beginning of the universe, the universe didn't exist. The Abyss is defined as that which doesn't exist. Therefore, before the beginning of the universe, the universe was part of the abyss.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where this breaks down, for me, is the very idea that the universe has to have a beginning at all. Pretty much every creation story begin with the premise that, while the world as we know it doesn't exist yet, there are still things that do, and which have a definite reality. It makes a lot of sense to me that, just as the biblical God was already there &quot;in the beginning,&quot; when the world was without form and void, the Supernal is eternal even if the physical world may not be.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Supernal didn't emerge from anything; the Superal is and was and will be, world without end and all that. Indeed, beginnings and endings are merely symbols which exist within the eternal truth that mages call the Supernal Realms.<br /> <br /> That being said, this in no way precludes the possibility that the Abyss can grant powers that would be impossible to replicate through Supernal magic. I'm fact, it *must* be true that there are abyssal spells and attainments - magics that never were and should never be, and which violate whatever transcendent principles define and govern the Supernal itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:14:52-08:00","id":1041989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041980#post1041980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where this breaks down, for me, is the very idea that the universe has to have a beginning at all. Pretty much every creation story begin with the premise that, while the world as we know it doesn't exist yet, there are still things that do, and which have a definite reality. It makes a lot of sense to me that, just as the biblical God was already there &quot;in the beginning,&quot; when the world was without form and void, the Supernal is eternal even if the physical world may not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition,<a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/supernal\" target=\"_blank\"> actual definition not mage definition</a>, the Supernal comes from the divine. It's possible these beings were just created through the Abyss like everything else was, and did something impossible like everything else does, they just managed to run with it. Or that they just found the Supernal watchtowers floating in the Abyss, gathered them together and knitted together the world. The Tremere bible, the Suspire, suggests that the watchtowers once existed in the Abyss and there's still more out there. If you want to dismiss that source, that's fine, but it is as credible as anything a mage has come up with.<br /> <br /> That said if you want a more-or-less logical argument for 'eternal Supernal' then you can point at the condition of the Fallen World. If our world, complete with Abyss, is the reflection of something greater, even greater than the Supernal, than our Supernal have been there ever since the reflection was made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said, this in no way precludes the possibility that the Abyss can grant powers that would be impossible to replicate through Supernal magic. I'm fact, it *must* be true that there are abyssal spells and attainments - magics that never were and should never be, and which violate whatever transcendent principles define and govern the Supernal itself. </div> </div> </div>That's a given, it's basically the reason people summon abyssal entities and make deals with them, it can do things Supernal magic can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:21:58-08:00","id":1041994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041980#post1041980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand it correctly, the idea that the universe (in the broadest possible sense) emerged from the Abyss goes something like this: &quot;before the beginning of the universe, the universe didn't exist. The Abyss is defined as that which doesn't exist. Therefore, before the beginning of the universe, the universe was part of the abyss.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss isn't non-existence. If the Supernal is a coherent set of concepts that generate the Fallen World, then the Abyss is the sum total of all possible concepts, the ones that don't make sense, contradict each other and are paradoxical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:25:46-08:00","id":1041997,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3209\" data-vbnamecard=\"3209\">CatDoom</a>. you literally have start of Bible in Genesis from the words:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></b></span></span>In the beginning God created the heavens and the earth. <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2 </span></b></span>Now the earth was formless and empty, darkness was over the surface of the deep, and the Spirit of God was hovering over the waters.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3 </span></b></span>And God said, \u201cLet there be light,\u201d and there was light. <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4 </span></b></span>God saw that the light was good, and he separated the light from the darkness.<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5 </span></b></span>God called the light \u201cday,\u201d and the darkness he called \u201cnight.\u201d And there was evening, and there was morning\u2014the first day.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> If this 'Darkness' is more 'universe-before-universe', you clearly have Abyss here described. Same is with Ginnungagap from Norse myths, bottomless abyss that was all there was prior to the <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/tales/norse-creation-myth/\" target=\"_blank\">beginning of the cosmos</a>, and into which the cosmos will collapse once again during <a href=\"http://norse-mythology.org/tales/ragnarok/\" target=\"_blank\">Ragnarok</a>, described in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041842#post1041842\">post here</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#767676\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:19px\">That was the age when nothing was;</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#767676\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:19px\">There was no sand, nor sea, nor cool waves,</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#767676\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:19px\">No earth nor sky nor grass there,</span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#767676\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Only Ginnungagap.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041980#post1041980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where this breaks down, for me, is the very idea that the universe has to have a beginning at all. Pretty much every creation story begin with the premise that, while the world as we know it doesn't exist yet, there are still things that do, and which have a definite reality. It makes a lot of sense to me that, just as the biblical God was already there &quot;in the beginning,&quot; when the world was without form and void, the Supernal is eternal even if the physical world may not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that 'are before universe' is clearly Abyss in this interpretation. Even if God exists in this 'world'/state, he IS part of it, is part of Abyss, as Abyss is everything before the world coming to being. That returns to our idea that Supernal is 'ordered' part of Abyss. 'God' is part of primordial Abyss that wanted to be ordered - or humanity's want to harness it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041980#post1041980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, the Supernal didn't emerge from anything; the Superal is and was and will be, world without end and all that. Indeed, beginnings and endings are merely symbols which exist within the eternal truth that mages call the Supernal Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-%E2%80%98growing%E2%80%99-with-humanity\">There are proofs that Supernal is evolving with humanity</a> - I think it's logical to say that Supernal was created by humanity, by the 'First Atlantis'. Or at least from sentience of humanity at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:54:49-08:00","id":1042054,"title":"","content":"I don' think the Supernal can be said to be evolving. It's probably more of a lateral development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:21:55-08:00","id":1042069,"title":"","content":"You know, all this claim about the Abyss somehow being the origin point of Creation, rather than a toxic External corruption <i>like it is right now</i>, makes for a great sales pitch for Scelesti-dom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your Outside is still about stillborn gods and corpses of world-progenitors, then you say the same as I think Primodrial in this sense. I.E. 'Place where universe as we know it started - and things that 'did not catch' with those that made Fallen World.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>No, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, the stillborn gods we forcefully label with something from Babylonian mythos because we can't quite grasp the concept of anti-existence are not Primordial (ie. the starting point of the universe and possibly its ending point as well), because they were never there in the first place. (continuing with the birth metaphor, that is)<br /> <br /> Pangu, the giant in Chinese mythos, was born from a cosmic egg. Ymir the first frost giant was born from The Gap. We never saw YHWH being born in the Genesis, because the Genesis is pretty much His autobiography, but He and the ocean on to which He breathed life into existed beforehand. All those things are Primordial, for they are the beginning points of existence.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is the Shortness and Longness lying outisde between the Fire and Ice. It could only associate with the Gap between Fire and Ice only after Ymir rose out of it.<br /> The Abyss is the Murk outside the Cosmic Egg. It could only cling onto the Mists of Creation inside the Egg only after Pangu hatched from it.<br /> The Abyss is the Stars above the Black Waters. It could only see the World below after YHWH Himself shaped the Waters into the World.<br /> <br /> Going with a SF metaphor, the Abyss is a Parasitic Alien from outer space that mutates and devours the lifeforms of our planet, not the Space Meteor whose shock jump-started the chemical process that formed the first biological molecule.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is not the Primordial Non-existence out of which Existence sprang from (huh, this reminds me of Taoism). It is Anti-existence, which look a lot like Non-existence from the POV of we who live in Existence, and the Abyss latches onto that resonance to claim a foothold in our world.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Scelesti would whisper otherwise......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  misspelling 02-01-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:07:12-08:00","id":1042099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1041989#post1041989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition,<a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/supernal\" target=\"_blank\"> actual definition not mage definition</a>, the Supernal comes from the divine. It's possible these beings were just created through the Abyss like everything else was, and did something impossible like everything else does, they just managed to run with it. Or that they just found the Supernal watchtowers floating in the Abyss, gathered them together and knitted together the world. The Tremere bible, the Suspire, suggests that the watchtowers once existed in the Abyss and there's still more out there. If you want to dismiss that source, that's fine, but it is as credible as anything a mage has come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kind of taking as proven that anything aside from the occasional relatively short-lived existential nightmare ever emerged from the Abyss at all. No actual evidence has ever been presented for this, aside from perhaps the unsubstantiated holy writ of one of the most twisted an pathetic groups of pseudo-immortals in the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things that 'are before universe' is clearly Abyss in this interpretation. Even if God exists in this 'world'/state, he IS part of it, is part of Abyss, as Abyss is everything before the world coming to being. That returns to our idea that Supernal is 'ordered' part of Abyss. 'God' is part of primordial Abyss that wanted to be ordered - or humanity's want to harness it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just my point: they're <i>not</i> &quot;before the universe&quot;; these myths suggest, essentially, that the universe was around already before the world we currently live in existed. The Bible talks about darkness and waters - these aren't weird, formless, indescribable things - they're not even the absence of things altogether. They're things that are still around in the world today - explicitly so, actually, since God makes night from the darkness that's already there, and makes seas from the water that's already there. If you want to see what this primordial universe was like you don't have to go to the Abyss, all you have to do is dive deep underwater without a light.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Ginnungagap lay between Niflheim and Muspelheim, two realms that are still around and very much real in the context of Norse mythology, and which are defined by heat and cold - two perfectly ordinary properties differentiated perhaps only in intensity from the heat and cold experienced by people in Midgard.<br /> <br /> There's a deeper issue I take with your reasoning though: If the Supernal is merely the &quot;ordered&quot; part of the Abyss, then the Fallen World, being explicitly a myth-of-the-cave style shadow of the Supernal, must be so too, as must, presumably, basically every other known part of the CoD universe. If that's the case, then the Abyss <i>is</i> the universe (as well as being the Abyss, to the extent that the Abyss can be said to not be part of the universe). Which may be exactly your point.<br /> <br /> But at that point I have to ask... so what? Calling the whole universe the Abyss, including those parts which do not have the properties normally associated with the Abyss, is basically just using a different word to refer to the same thing. It would necessitate that we come up with some other term to refer to what is currently referred to as the Abyss, since it's a qualitatively different part of the universe when compared to the rest of it. And now we're just playing with semantics, and haven't actually learned anything at all about the nature of reality in the CoD universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-%E2%80%98growing%E2%80%99-with-humanity\">There are proofs that Supernal is evolving with humanity</a> - I think it's logical to say that Supernal was created by humanity, by the 'First Atlantis'. Or at least from sentience of humanity at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting hypothesis, and the observation that human beings can add symbols to the Supernal Realms (maybe, assuming that's actually what's going on) <i>could</i> imply that humanity collectively created the Supernal, but it does not <i>necessarily </i>follow from that observation, or even that it's the most likely conclusion to reach. After all, the fact that the faces of four American presidents are carved into Mount Rushmore doesn't imply that Americans built the mountain itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:13:26-08:00","id":1042124,"title":"","content":"Time is part of the universe. There was no &quot;before&quot; the universe because the very concept of &quot;before&quot; came into being right along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:30:29-08:00","id":1042128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042124#post1042124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time is part of the universe. There was no &quot;before&quot; the universe because the very concept of &quot;before&quot; came into being right along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a big part of why it's impossible to explain what came &quot;before the big bang&quot; IRL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:34:56-08:00","id":1042181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042054#post1042054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don' think the Supernal can be said to be evolving. It's probably more of a lateral development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree but it's the Free Council's belief, and just latching onto the beliefs of the Diamond Orders is a kind of trap.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's likely to gain more traction here than, 'The Watchtowers were idigam.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T23:18:42-08:00","id":1042247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042099#post1042099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a deeper issue I take with your reasoning though: If the Supernal is merely the &quot;ordered&quot; part of the Abyss, then the Fallen World, being explicitly a myth-of-the-cave style shadow of the Supernal, must be so too, as must, presumably, basically every other known part of the CoD universe. If that's the case, then the Abyss <i>is</i> the universe (as well as being the Abyss, to the extent that the Abyss can be said to not be part of the universe). Which may be exactly your point.<br /> <br /> But at that point I have to ask... so what? Calling the whole universe the Abyss, including those parts which do not have the properties normally associated with the Abyss, is basically just using a different word to refer to the same thing. It would necessitate that we come up with some other term to refer to what is currently referred to as the Abyss, since it's a qualitatively different part of the universe when compared to the rest of it. And now we're just playing with semantics, and haven't actually learned anything at all about the nature of reality in the CoD universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's <b>exactly</b> my point - in Mage, whole universe can be said to be in Abyss. They are just some more 'ordered' parts of it. And no, I do not think that all those Scelesti seeking other solutions OR simply trying to understand universe, would agree 'it's just semantics'. Now I have image of Mystygoug mage that after years of researching Supernal Realms finally understood everything is in Abyss all along... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042099#post1042099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting hypothesis, and the observation that human beings can add symbols to the Supernal Realms (maybe, assuming that's actually what's going on) <i>could</i> imply that humanity collectively created the Supernal, but it does not <i>necessarily </i>follow from that observation, or even that it's the most likely conclusion to reach. After all, the fact that the faces of four American presidents are carved into Mount Rushmore doesn't imply that Americans built the mountain itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>'You can stick with you Diamond shortsightedness that Supernal is everlasting! We know magic comes from humanity!' &lt;Takes his toys and runs to his nearest Assembly to share the lore with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042124#post1042124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time is part of the universe. There was no &quot;before&quot; the universe because the very concept of &quot;before&quot; came into being right along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ruins of Time <i>Before</i> seems to not agree with you on that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:09:16-08:00","id":1042261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042181#post1042181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree but it's the Free Council's belief, and just latching onto the beliefs of the Diamond Orders is a kind of trap.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's likely to gain more traction here than, 'The Watchtowers were idigam.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the FC believe that humanity changes the Supernal, but that still isn't the same as evolution of it. Like I said it's a lateral development so more like water into ice and ice into a sculpture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:42:54-08:00","id":1042265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042247#post1042247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ruins of Time <i>Before</i> seems to not agree with you on that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If we go into real philosophy here: it's a question of semantics, but Elfive is right and the book is wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Per definition there cannot be anything &quot;before&quot; or &quot;after&quot; if no time exists. Time exists because of the expansion of space. So there can be something <i>outside</i> of time, but not before. Tachyons from the big bang, if they exist, would be an example.<br /> <br /> Back to the creation myth of CoD. I honestly din't read into this, but what I can fathom from this thread gives a couple of logical problems. If the Supernal is basically the sum of everything that can be (can come or is in existence) and the Abyss is the sum of everything that cannot be (is contrary to existence), the Supernal cannot logically have emerged from the Abyss. What might have happened is that before existence, there was a state of every concept that can be and cannot be together (Supernal + Abyss) and as the first act of creation those two split from each other into the Abyss and the Supernal. This is in fact pretty much the base line for <i>every</i> creation myth, that ever existed. It has also to be noted, that it is impossible to define &quot;what cannot be&quot; without defining &quot;what can be&quot; so before the split, there cannot have been an Abyss nor the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 02-02-2017, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:58:45-08:00","id":1042268,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11939\" data-vbnamecard=\"11939\">HardcoreHannes</a> actually, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> is just misinterpreting Time Before, which just means the time before the fall, not events transpiring before time began. So no, the book isn't wrong,and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:05:08-08:00","id":1042271,"title":"","content":"Fine with me either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:38:38-08:00","id":1042280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042265#post1042265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the creation myth of CoD. I honestly din't read into this, but what I can fathom from this thread gives a couple of logical problems. If the Supernal is basically the sum of everything that can be (can come or is in existence) and the Abyss is the sum of everything that cannot be (is contrary to existence), the Supernal cannot logically have emerged from the Abyss. What might have happened is that before existence, there was a state of every concept that can be and cannot be together (Supernal + Abyss) and as the first act of creation those two split from each other into the Abyss and the Supernal. This is in fact pretty much the base line for <i>every</i> creation myth, that ever existed. It has also to be noted, that it is impossible to define &quot;what cannot be&quot; without defining &quot;what can be&quot; so before the split, there cannot have been an Abyss nor the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can go with that Abyss+Supernal were one 'on the beginning', as it's basically what was proposed earlier. Just Scelesti likes to reduce Abyss+Supernal = Abyss 'on the beginning', as it is still contrary to proper being. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:02:55-08:00","id":1042287,"title":"","content":"It is still significantly different, since it can be argued, that all the &quot;right&quot; stuff split from everything and formed the Supernal, while all the &quot;wrong&quot; stuff formed the Abyss. If the the Supernal just emerged as some kind of proper concept from the Abyss it would mean that a different, completely viable Truth might emerge from the Abyss again. While if every possible truth already split from what the Abyss is now, nothing possible remains, which concludes that only unmaking can come from the Abyss but no existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:10:08-08:00","id":1042290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042280#post1042280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I can go with that Abyss+Supernal were one 'on the beginning', as it's basically what was proposed earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this I agree with as well. Never understood why you insisted on this &quot;Abyss on the beginning&quot; be the same thing with the Abyss.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Secret Order of the Gate, who seem to be the only Scelesti group out to figure out the cosmic importance of the Abyss rather than just drawing power from it, claim that the Abyss is the Serpent who devours the World-Tree bit by bit so that it does not grow too much and disturb the Heavens Above (ie. the Supernal). From this line of thought, I can see some Scelesi claiming that the Abyss is the Purifier that purges the World into its pristine, Primordial state, rather than saying it's the Primodial Soup itself.<br /> <br /> It also comes to mind that what I just described is basically the Wyrm's original cosmic role back in WoD. And there was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/809400-umaraha-e-the-children-of-the-worm\">this homebrew </a>made by Claire Redfield way back. Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:28:04-08:00","id":1042569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042247#post1042247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's <b>exactly</b> my point - in Mage, whole universe can be said to be in Abyss. They are just some more 'ordered' parts of it. And no, I do not think that all those Scelesti seeking other solutions OR simply trying to understand universe, would agree 'it's just semantics'. Now I have image of Mystygoug mage that after years of researching Supernal Realms finally understood everything is in Abyss all along... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm imagining it now:<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti (Scelestus?):</b> Fool! All that is is part of the Abyss!<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacle Mage:</b> Erm... ok, let's say I believe that. What does that even mean?<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti:</b> It means I rule you! Mwahahahaha!<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacle Mage:</b> (sets the cackling Scelesti on fire and watches him run around screaming) You know, I think there may be a flaw in your reasoning...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:15:10-08:00","id":1042599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041713-truth-in-mage-and-d-d-planes?p=1042569#post1042569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm imagining it now:<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti (Scelestus?):</b> Fool! All that is is part of the Abyss!<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacle Mage:</b> Erm... ok, let's say I believe that. What does that even mean?<br /> <br /> <b>Scelesti:</b> It means I rule you! Mwahahahaha!<br /> <br /> <b>Pentacle Mage:</b> (sets the cackling Scelesti on fire and watches him run around screaming) You know, I think there may be a flaw in your reasoning...</div> </div> </div> </div>(Correct singular form is 'Scelestus' )<br /> <br /> Ending would be different:<br /> <br /> Pentacle Mage : (sets the cackling Scelesti on fire and watches him run around screaming) You know, I think there may be a flaw in your reasoning...<br /> <br /> Scelestus starts to laugh himself as Supernal fire is <i>healing</i> him. Then he summons Gulmoth and sends on Pentacle Mage, as he can use however many Paradox Reaches if he wants. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T14:50:02-08:00","id":1042615,"title":"","content":"Again though, even if we except that the entire cosmos is the Abyss... There's still a part of the Abyss that behaves differently than the rest of the Abyss, and we need something to call that. For the sake of argument, let's call it the Negaverse. So, now that we're &quot;correctly&quot; referring to the cosmos as the Abyss and the part of the Abyss that causes Paradox the Negaverse, what practical difference does this revelation make? The relationship between the Abyss and the Negaverse is exactly the same as the relationship between the cosmos and the Abyss, so all we've done is changed the names. At this point someone might even raise the argument that if everything in the Abyss arose from the Negaverse, we should be calling the entire Abyss the Negaverse, and the Negaverse something else, like Guinungagap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:12:33-08:00","id":1042625,"title":"","content":"Come on, Negaverse? You might as well name it Evilville. Just call one Abyss and one Abyss Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T15:14:57-08:00","id":1042628,"title":"","content":"I mean. I think cosmos and Abyss work fine. That was kinda the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:24:53-08:00","id":1042693,"title":"","content":"At this point I'm honestly curious and baffled - what's the meaning of all this?<br /> <br /> Some mages in the past decided to name the not-yet-named toxic anti-reality from outside proper reality with the names of the primordial progenitors of the world from their own cultural mythologies, because that's honestly what it seems to look like back then.<br /> <br /> It's like claiming Indians (Native Americans) really are from India, just because some Europeans in the past decided to call them Indians because they believed they were from India. And after a nuclear apocalypse or something, researchers in the far future dig up our age's documents, and think Indians are a really well-traveled people who lived on two continents at once.<br /> <br /> Sharing names does not make two things the same. Sure, maybe they were named that way in the first place because they had common characteristics, but that's where the similarity ends.<br /> <br /> If we can claim the Abyss is the alpha-and-omega of the world because people named it after the primordial forces of the world which it shares common behavioral patterns with, then why can't we just go back to the old Arcadia Problem? Or better yet, claim all the Acathartoi, Abyssal Intruders, Goetic Demons, Pandemonic Entities, and the Unchained are from the same source because they're all called &quot;demons?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:40:59-08:00","id":1042844,"title":"","content":"By going with <b>Left Hand Path</b> book on sorcerers from Kish...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LHP, p. 63</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consumed with the desire to rebuild what they lost, the rest of the Atlantean Diaspora paid little attention to the Scelesti. Only Accursed armies laying siege to their eldritch fortresses inspired them to march forth. They repelled the Kishites using their enemies\u2019 methods. In Akkad, Ur, and Larsa, they said they represented new gods, willing to fight Kish\u2019s aggression. <br /> Under Awakened guidance, these city-states vanquished Kish\u2019s warrior-demoniacs and Wicked princes. The spiritual ancestors of Pentacle and Throne mages founded Kish anew and rewrote its legends. The old lords became Tiamat\u2019s children, fated to be crushed by Anu, Marduk and the other gods of civilization.<br /> <br /> Organized Scelesti use titles and customs inspired by the legends of old Kish, though they freely admit that reconstructions have eclipsed true lineages. The Accursed believe the Kishite eon gave <i>all</i> mages new life\u2014without it, the Awakened would have cowered in their ruined outposts, leaving bones and curios for a world without the Pentacle. The Scelesti summoned them from hermitage and taught them how to survive the Fallen age by guiding Sleepers. To some of the Wicked, this justifies every sorcerer or Sleeper they corrupt. They have given something immeasurable to the world, and they deserve their reward.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LHP, p. 63</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scelesti say that the Abyss has always existed and al-ways will. It was no more created by the Fall than the ocean is created by the fish that swim within it. Frightened mages would believe that sorcery made the Void in the hope that spells can contain it. They want to think the Abyss is a thin membrane of countermagic, and that Paradoxes are mere side effects\u2014terrified nonsense from limited thinkers. All sorcery is invasion, contradiction. Supernal principles penetrate Fallen existence. The Abyss is no barrier to magic, but rather the primal violation that rips open one reality to let another in. Paradox is the true face of sorcery when it works its will without stultifying Supernal restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>And...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LHP, p. 63</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Alethians</b><br /> To many Scelesti, the Abyss is a realm of unbounded possibility. Within the true Tellurian, every phenomenon obeys forms and laws. Beyond the prison, the Abyss supplies power and comfort to those willing to confront it. By refusing to obey desires completely, the Tellurian regulates them, encouraging a controlled, socially acceptable self-image. When a mage refuses the Abyss she blinds herself to the consequences of a realm that satisfies her true feelings, beyond the Lie\u2019s programming.<br /> <br /> Alethian doctrine is probably the most successful in attracting recruits because of the wish fulfillment angle. Willworkers tend to overestimate their self-awareness and unknowingly suppress darker urges. Even after initiation, Alethian Scelesti blend in with other mages as long as they can hide disgusting appetites the Abyss helped them discover.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T04:45:51-08:00","id":1042885,"title":"","content":"Okay, so we have...<br /> <br /> 1) Self-proclaimed descendants of Kish who thinks all the other mages owe them big time, because they inspired them to get off their lazy asses and become a united force. That's like an imperialist arguing that it was the ruthless, bloody imperialist expansions that triggered the rise of nationalism, so that all nation-states owe them for their conception. Which... isn't wrong, but not right neither.<br /> <br /> 2) I think the key point here is &quot;The Scelesti say.&quot; We're talking about people who degraded the essence of their self-being and denied all that they stand for (Abyssal Joining), or people who shaped their soul into resonating with Abyssal Entities (Abyssal Legacies). I wouldn't take philosophy or cosmology lessons from them, for the same reason I wouldn't take ethics lessons from the Joker. (Of course, I'd be a hypocrite if I didn't admit that things would get very interesting if we do...)<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, the Abyss grants impossibilities, and with that Alethian Scelesti can do things normal mages simply can't. That part I always agreed with - it's the reason why Abyssal dealings are so tempting in the first place! However, that still doesn't mean the Abyss is the same thing as the primordial soup, which contains (or contained) all the possiblities of the world, not its impossibilities. In this vein, you and I could agree that the Abyss is what's left of the Primordial, after all its possibilities pooled into the Supernal. It is a hollow, empty husk - what the Kabbalah calls the Qlippoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:24:14-08:00","id":1042933,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts about the original topic.<br /> <br /> 1) The Supernal's analog would actually lie with the Inner Planes instead of any of the Outer Planes. Tradiitionally speaking, the Inner Planes serve as the source for most wizard's magic. The five Paths reflect different &quot;elemental&quot; magics that aren't just tied to elements, but rather concepts like Energy, Life, Space, etc. Yes, I know there's differences between the classic elements and five Paths, but if we look at the role they play in the two different stories, we find similarities.<br /> <br /> 2) The original conversation was about the Abyss in the two different games having similar stories and roles when taking apart from their respective cosmologies. Irregardless if its true that either Abyss gave birth to the rest of the cosmos is immaterial - stories exist in both games to give plot hooks, not absolute answers. But they are both filled with toxic entities and energies that thrive on destructive actions, and are often described as profane and inflicting madness (see the latest Out of the Abyss storyline in D&amp;D for more on that). And it should be noted that the original Abomination gods (like the Cthulhu-copy) were actually found inside the Abyss and not the Far Realm. They don't get as much spotlight as they used to, but they're still there.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm liking the comparison between the Nine Hells and the Exarchs more and more as time goes on. There's not exactly a blood war going on between them, but the Exarchs have been known to put the Abyss back in its cage a time or two. And the whole tyranny thing meshes better with D&amp;D than I find the Inferno (just feeding on sin) does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}